# What NOT to ship in the VSIX.
#
# Keep in mind what IS required at runtime, and must never be excluded:
#   out/**      the extension host entry (package.json "main")
#   dist/**     the esbuild-bundled webview scripts + css
#   resources/  the activity-bar icon, the marketplace icon, and the agent's
#               status icons (loaded at runtime via asWebviewUri)
#   syntaxes/, language-configuration.json  the .rqml language contribution

# ── Sources and build inputs ───────────────────────────────────────────
src/**
**/*.ts
**/*.tsx
**/*.map
**/tsconfig.json
**/eslint.config.mjs
esbuild.js

# webview-ui is a build INPUT only: esbuild bundles it into dist/. Shipping the
# directory shipped its entire node_modules (mermaid, react, cytoscape demo
# GIFs) — 4,201 files and ~57 MB, the single largest thing in the package.
webview-ui/**

# README images are rewritten to raw.githubusercontent.com by the
# --baseImagesUrl flag in the package/publish scripts, so the marketplace page
# never reads these from inside the VSIX.
images/**

# ── Dead weight inside production dependencies ─────────────────────────
# None of these are reachable at runtime; they are build artifacts, test
# fixtures and documentation that the upstream packages happen to publish.
# ~5 MB, dominated by pdfkit shipping a full Yarn release binary.
node_modules/**/.yarn/**
node_modules/**/test/__snapshots__/**
node_modules/ai/docs/**

# ── Tooling and local config ───────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode/**
.vscode-test/**
**/.vscode-test.*
.gitignore
.yarnrc
.npmrc
vsc-extension-quickstart.md
AGENTS.md
README-AGENT.md

# Compiled tests and their fixtures — built by `compile`, never used at runtime.
out/test/**
